Month = {MAR-MAY},
Abstract = {In this article the author argues that we need not just to decolonize'
   the Anthropocene but also to desecularize' it - to be aware that in the
   new age of the Earth we may be coeval with gods and spirits. Drawing
   particularly on the work of Gilles Deleuze, Felix Guattari and Georges
   Bataille, and using concepts from both thermodynamics and fluid
   dynamics, the author starts to develop an interdisciplinary theory of
   planetary spirit and use this to speak of both the laminar' high gods of
   time that are being invoked to summon the story of Earth's ongoing
   transformation into a canonical mythos, and the turbulent lower spirits
   of place which manifest particular, situated dynamics on an Earth
   crossed by interlocking gradients and flows of energy, value, power and
   entropy. He suggests that what might once have been distinct
   territorialized cultures' or natures' in which humans engaged in
   particular situated patterns of interaction with animals, spirits and
   other beings are increasingly being convened into a global multinatural
   system.},
